schema: "0.4"
id: fim-math-and-scientific-rendering-chemdraw-js-03-editor-3d-integration
type: interactive
quality: high
solution: chemdraw-js
category: math-and-scientific-rendering
variant: editor-3d-integration
references:
- references/fim/solution/chemdraw-js.md
- references/fim/use-case/mathematical-scientific.md
prompt:
  system: |-
    You are a senior web chemistry application engineer. Output only one complete ASCII HTML document with inline CSS and JavaScript. Prefer Ketcher, RDKit.js, and 3Dmol.js integration patterns; do not assume commercial ChemDraw JS availability. No Markdown fences or prose outside the artifact.
  text: |-
    Create an interactive molecule editing and 3D handoff prototype.

    Scenario:
    Build a browser artifact that embeds a Ketcher-style editor panel, synchronizes the current molecule to RDKit.js for 2D SVG plus descriptors, and sends a MOL/SDF representation into 3Dmol.js for a 3D stick/sphere preview.

    Requirements:
    - Use Ketcher APIs as asynchronous operations: setMolecule, getSmiles, getMolfile, and getKet must be awaited or represented as awaited integration calls.
    - Include a fallback path for environments where Ketcher assets are unavailable: provide a textarea for SMILES/MOL input and render with RDKit.js instead of failing blank.
    - Initialize a sample molecule, caffeine, and allow switching to ethanol, benzene, and aspirin.
    - Use RDKit.js to validate current SMILES, render a 2D SVG, and compute descriptors.
    - Use 3Dmol.js to create a viewer, addModel with sdf or mol data, setStyle with stick and sphere, zoomTo, and render.
    - Include visible async state for editor loading, molecule sync, RDKit validation, descriptor extraction, 3D model load, and 3D render completion.
    - Include a clear warning that ChemDraw JS is commercial and this artifact uses open web chemistry fallbacks.
    - Clean up RDKit WASM objects and dispose or reset 3D viewer state between molecule changes where practical.
    - Include keyboard-operable controls, accessible status text, and a non-3D fallback summary.
    - Output only the final HTML artifact.
  provider_options:
    max_tokens: 10000
    temperature: 0.25
output:
  text_format: html
  artifact_kind: ketcher-rdkit-3dmol-integration-prototype
  formats:
  - format: html
  - format: svg
  render_expectation: Interactive chemistry editor prototype with 2D validation, descriptor panel, and 3Dmol.js preview or fallback.
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - "YAML parses and generated output is one complete ASCII HTML artifact."
  - "Ketcher integration is modeled with awaited async methods for setMolecule, getSmiles, getMolfile, and getKet."
  - "The artifact has a graceful fallback when Ketcher assets or commercial ChemDraw JS are unavailable."
  - "RDKit.js validates the current molecule, renders 2D SVG, computes descriptors, and deletes WASM objects."
  - "3Dmol.js creates a viewer, adds mol or sdf data, applies stick/sphere style, zooms, and renders."
  - "Async status states are visible for editor load, sync, validation, descriptors, 3D load, and render completion."
  - "Keyboard, text fallback, and accessibility requirements remain usable without WebGL."
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Generated HTML, CSS, and JavaScript are structurally valid and can load the referenced open chemistry libraries."
    - "Async Ketcher calls and 3Dmol.js viewer calls follow the referenced API shape."
    - "The artifact does not require commercial ChemDraw JS for the main workflow."
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Editor, RDKit validation, 2D rendering, descriptor extraction, and 3D preview are all represented."
    - "Sample molecule switching and fallback text input paths are present."
    - "The artifact makes the commercial/open-source distinction explicit."
  - name: Visual/structural quality
    weight: 25
    criteria:
    - "The editor, 2D, descriptor, and 3D panes are organized without overlap."
    - "Status labels and fallback messages are concise, visible, and useful for debugging."
    - "The 3D view is initialized with a nonblank background and framed molecule when data is valid."
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    criteria:
    - "Handles missing Ketcher assets, invalid molecule data, RDKit load failure, missing WebGL, and 3D model parse failure."
    - "Cleans up RDKit objects and resets stale viewer state between molecule changes."
    - "Keeps text and 2D summaries available when 3D rendering fails."
  pass_conditions:
  - "Rubric weights are exactly Format validity 30, Semantic completeness 30, Visual/structural quality 25, and Robustness 15."
  - "Score is 80 or higher out of 100 with no critical failure in async editor integration, RDKit validation, or 3Dmol render flow."
  - "The artifact demonstrates editor, 2D, descriptor, and 3D output spaces for the chemdraw-js solution family."
tags:
- fim
- math-and-scientific-rendering
- chemdraw-js
- ketcher
- rdkit-js
- 3dmol-js
- molecule-editor
- molecule-3d
- integration
